		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-22T00:51:05Z",
			"File": [
				"⡟⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				751,
				114
			],
			"Message": "style(Output): Normalize esbuild output with helpers-first ordering and 2-space indent\n\nRe-align all compiled artifacts under Configuration/ to a consistent esbuild output format. Three structural changes across the 100+ files in Apply, ESBuild, Plugin, Polyfill, Service, and Transform directories:\n\n1. Hoist `__defProp`/`__name` helper shim declarations above all static import statements, reverting the imports-first ordering applied in 88983f8. The helpers-first preamble avoids a forward-reference hazard when the shim variables are referenced at module-eval time inside collapsed arrow functions.\n\n2. Convert indentation back to 2-space (matching the Source/ TypeScript originals) from the tab style applied in 88983f8. Tabs produced narrower diffs against upstream VS Code but broke the visual alignment between compiled output and the authored TypeScript that the transform plugins pattern-match against.\n\n3. Normalise expression formatting: collapse multi-line arrow function bodies and object property values to single-line where line length permits, strip trailing commas from final array/object entries, consolidate empty function bodies, and format export blocks with one binding per line.\n\nNo runtime behaviour changes; the polyfill shims (Process, FileSystem, IPC, NativeModule, ChildProcess, SharedProcess), service stubs (NullTelemetry, NullUpdate, NullExtensionGallery), copy plugins, and transform pipelines (Replace, Rewrite, Inject, Strip, Patch, Instrument) are semantically identical before and after.",
			"SHA": "e2bbb5e89de3930893ccbdb5797e810be9ca8c49"
		},
